{
  "schema": 1,
  "about": [
    "Look templates for footage with no reference. Each template says what the look does to a picture:",
    "contrast: ratio of the tonal spread. floor: black level in DaVinci Intermediate (null keeps the footage's own).",
    "tints: [hue in degrees, amount] added to near-neutral tones per zone. Hue: red 0, yellow 60, green 120, cyan 180, blue 240, magenta 300.",
    "saturation: color level against the balanced footage (1.0 keeps it). rolloff: saturation left in deep shadows and bright highlights.",
    "hue_vs_sat, hue_vs_hue: optional palette points [hue, value]. mono: true removes all color.",
    "base and suits: the score. base plus weight times trait, each trait runs 0..1:",
    "skin, sky, foliage, daylight, low_key, high_key, flat, contrasty, colorful, muted, warm, cool."
  ],
